egeShine","description":"Arul Anandar College is a jesuit (roman catholic) arts & science college in Karumathur, Madurai established in 1970. Work, Justice & Love Check courses.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arul-Anandar-College-Karumathur-Madurai-_66_11zon.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Arul Anandar College","shortName":"AAC","tagline":"Work, Justice & Love","category":"arts-science","type":"Autonomous-Aided","ownership":"Jesuit (Roman Catholic)","established":1970,"location":"Karumathur, Madurai","district":"Madurai","address":"Karumathur, Madurai, Tamil Nadu - 625514","mapLink":"https://maps.google.com/?q=Arul+Anandar+College+Karumathur+Madurai)","mapQuery":"Arul Anandar College Karumathur Madurai","website":"https://www.aactni.edu.in/]","phone":"04549-287221","email":"principal@aactni.edu.in","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arul-Anandar-College-Karumathur-Madurai-_66_11zon.webp","videoUrl":null,"affiliation":"Madurai Kamaraj University, Madurai","accreditation":["NAAC Grade A","Autonomous Status","UGC 2f & 12B","MKU Affiliated"],"about":"Arul Anandar College (AAC) is a reputed autonomous co-educational institution situated in Karumathur, Madurai, administered by the Jesuits. Founded in 1970 and named after the Jesuit saint John de Britto (''Filled with Grace''), the college operates on the motto ''Work, Justice, and Love''. Set in a sprawling rural campus, it caters significantly to the educational empowerment of weaker sections, MBCs, and Scheduled Castes.\\n\\nThe college achieved autonomous status in 1987 and received NAAC ''A'' grade accreditation. AAC offers extensive undergraduate, postgraduate, and doctoral programs across arts, sciences, commerce, computer applications, and specialized rural development sciences, equipped with modern computer labs, an indoor stadium, a biometric library, 