urses and gradually expanded its academic portfolio to include undergraduate, postgraduate and research programmes. The institution has been functioning from its permanent campus at Thadangam since 1 November 1974, on approximately 42 acres of land. The college was initially affiliated to the University of Madras and has been functioning under Periyar University, Salem since 1998-99. It received NAAC B Grade in its first accreditation cycle and B++ Grade in the second cycle in April 2017.\\n\\nGovernment Arts College, Dharmapuri currently provides 22 undergraduate courses, 13 postgraduate courses, 10 M.Phil programmes and 6 Ph.D research programmes. The official college website states that more than 7,000 students are studying in the institution and that the college produces more than 1,500 graduates every year. The college provides academic departments across Arts, Science, Commerce and Management and supports students through hostels, laboratories, library facilities, health centre, transport, sports, NSS, NCC, placement and research-related activities.","highlights":["Established in 1965","42.12-acre permanent campus","NAAC B++ Grade","UGC 2(f) and 12(B) recognized","Affiliated to Periyar University, Salem","22 Undergraduate Courses","13 Postgraduate Courses","10 M.Phil Research Courses","6 Ph.D Research Courses","7000+ Students","1500+ Graduates Every Year","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution"],"departments":[{"name":"Tamil","level":"PhD"},{"name":"English","level":"PhD"},{"name":"History","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Political Science","level":"UG"},{"name":"Psychology","level":"UG"},{"name":"Social Work","level":"UG"},{"name":"Fashion Technology","level":"UG"},{"name":"Visual Communication","level":"UG"},{"name":"Economics","level":"UG"},{"name":"Mathematics","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Physics","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Chemistry","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Botany","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Zoology","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Computer Science","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Electronics & Communication","level":"UG"},{"name":"Statistics","level":"PhD"},{"name":"B.C.A","level":"UG"},{"name":"Commerce","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Commerce (Computer Application)","level":"PG"},{"name":"Co-Operation","level":"PG"},{"name":"Business Administration","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Campus Networking"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"Central Library"},{"icon":"ti-desktop","name":"Computer Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-flask","name":"Science Laboratories"},{"icon":"ti-world","name":"English Language Lab"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"BC/MBC Boys Hostel"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"BC/MBC Girls Hostel"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"SC/ST Boys Hostel"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"SC/ST Girls Hostel"},{"icon":"ti-heartbeat","name":"Health Centre"},{"icon":"ti-bus","name":"Transport Facility"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports Ground"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Seminar Hall"},{"icon":"ti-building","name":"Open Auditorium"},{"icon":"ti-sun","name":"Solar Plant"},{"icon":"ti-water","name":"Water Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-female","name":"Women Rest Room"}],"placementRate":"89%","avgPackage":"≈₹60,000 ","highestPackage":"≈₹70,000 ","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Online Registration","desc":"Applicants can register through the Tamil Nadu Government Arts and Science Colleges Admission portal for UG programmes."},{"title":"Eligibility","desc":"Candidates must satisfy the prescribed Higher Secondary qualification and programme-specific eligibility requirements."},{"title":"Rank List","desc":"Eligible applications are processed according to qualifying examination marks and Government reservation norms."},{"title":"Counselling","desc":"Candidates participate in the counselling process and select available courses according to rank, category and vacancy."},{"title":"Document Verification","desc":"Selected candidates submit original academic, transfer, community and other required certificates for verification."},{"title":"Fee Payment","desc":