('arignar-anna-government-arts-college-attur','arignar-anna-government-arts-college-attur','Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai)','AAGAC Attur','arts-science','Degree College','Government','1972','Vadachennimalai, Attur','Salem','Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Vadachennimalai, Attur - 636121, Salem District, Tamil Nadu, India','https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arignar+Anna+Government+Arts+College+Attur+Vadachennimalai','https://www.aagacattur.org.in/',' 04282 - 235001','aagacattur@yahoo.co.in','https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp','Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur - CollegeShine','Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai) is a government arts & science college in Vadachennimalai, Attur established in 1972. Duty.',NULL, '{"id":"arignar-anna-government-arts-college-attur","seo":{"metaTitle":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur - CollegeShine","metaDescription":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai) is a government arts & science college in Vadachennimalai, Attur established in 1972. Duty.","metaKeywords":["Arignar Anna Government Arts College","Attur (Vadachennimalai)","AAGAC Attur","Arignar Anna Government Arts College","Attur (Vadachennimalai) admission 2026","Arignar Anna Government Arts College","Attur (Vadachennimalai) fees","Arignar Anna Government Arts College","Attur (Vadachennimalai) courses","Arts & Science colleges in Salem","Vadachennimalai","Attur","Salem","Arts & Science","Government","Degree College","NAAC B (28-02-2005)"],"canonicalUrl":null,"robots":"index, follow","h1":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai)","openGraph":{"title":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur - CollegeShine","description":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai) is a government arts & science college in Vadachennimalai, Attur established in 1972. Duty.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur - CollegeShine","description":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai) is a government arts & science college in Vadachennimalai, Attur established in 1972. Duty.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Attur (Vadachennimalai)","shortName":"AAGAC Attur","tagline":"Duty, Dignity and Discipline at the foothills of Vadachennimalai","category":"arts-science","type":"Degree College","ownership":"Government","established":"1972","location":"Vadachennimalai, Attur","district":"Salem","address":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Vadachennimalai, Attur - 636121, Salem District, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arignar+Anna+Government+Arts+College+Attur+Vadachennimalai","mapQuery":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Vadachennimalai, Attur, Salem, Tamil Nadu 636121","website":"https://www.aagacattur.org.in/","phone":" 04282 - 235001","email":"aagacattur@yahoo.co.in","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/qrKIH4RjZZw?si=GIj7ItsRQ-bZonCB","affiliation":"Periyar University, Salem","accreditation":["NAAC B (28-02-2005)"],"about":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College is situated at the foothills of Vadachennimalai (North Chenni Hill), a small hill near Attur associated with Lord Bala Thandayuthapani, and is circumfused by the Kalvarayan hills and Vasishta river to the north and the Kolli-Pachamalai hills and Vellar river to the south. The foundation stone for its building was laid in March 1972 by then-Governor K.K. Shah, and the college was formally opened in October 1973 by minister K. Rajaram. Though originally established for men, women students were admitted from 1975 onward, making it a co-educational institution. The college was affiliated to Periyar University, Salem in 1998-99 and was accredited with a ''B'' grade by NAAC in February 2005.\\n\\nNamed after C.N. Annadurai (Arignar Anna), the former Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu whose guiding principles were Duty, Dignity and Discipline, the college sits on an expansive 128-acre (50-hectare) campus with roughly 6,300 square metres of built-up area. It offers programmes across Tamil, History and other arts and science disciplines, including M.Phil research options, and continues to serve the rural communities of the Kalvarayan and Kolli hills region surrounding Attur.","highlights":["Foundation laid 1972, opened 1973; named after Arignar Anna","Affiliated to Periyar University, Salem since 1998-99","NAAC B grade accredited (2005)","Spread over 128 acres (50 hectares) at the foothills of Vadachennimalai","Became co-educational from 1975"],"departments":[{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"}],"facilities":["Library","Hostel","Computer Literacy Programme (CLP)","Soft Skills Development","Entrepreneurship Development Programme (EDP)","OSA","Parent Teacher Association (PTA)","Canteen","Placement Cell","Sports Facilities"],"placementRate":4.7,"avgPackage":"~ ₹3 LPA ","highestPackage":"~ ₹3.5 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":["Merit-based admission per Tamil Nadu Government / TNGASA norms","10+2 pass required for UG entry"],"scholarships":["Scholarship facility is available","Scholarship support is listed among the college facilities"],"events":["College events are conducted throughout the academic year"],"distanceInfo":{"status":"Distance information is currently being updated"},"hostelFeatures":["Hostel details are currently being updated"],"technicalClubs":["Technical club information is currently being updated"],"culturalClubs":["Fine Arts","College Union","Rotaract"],"communityService":["NSS","Red Ribbon Club (RRC)"]}'),
('government-arts-college-women-salem','government-arts-college-women-salem','Government Arts College for Women, Salem','GACW Salem','arts-science','Degree College (Women)','Government','1972','Gorimedu, Salem','Salem','Government Arts College for Women, Yercaud Main Road, Gorimedu, Salem - 636008, Tamil Nadu, India','https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Government+Arts+College+for+Women+Salem','https://govtwomencollegeslm8.org/',NULL,NULL,'https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Women-Salem-collegshine_2_11zon.webp','Government Arts College for Women, Salem | Salem - CollegeShine','Government Arts College for Women, Salem is a government arts & science college in Gorimedu, Salem established in 1972. The only government women''s college.',NULL, '{"id":"government-arts-college-women-salem","seo":{"metaTitle":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem | Salem - CollegeShine","metaDescription":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem is a government arts & science college in Gorimedu, Salem established in 1972. The only government women''s college.","metaKeywords":["Government Arts College for Women","Salem","GACW Salem","Government Arts College for Women","Salem admission 2026","Government Arts College for Women","Salem fees","Government Arts College for Women","Salem courses","Arts & Science colleges in Salem","Gorimedu","Salem","Salem","Arts & Science","Government","Degree College (Women)","NAAC A (3rd Cycle","Re-accredited)"],"canonicalUrl":null,"robots":"index, follow","h1":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem","openGraph":{"title":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem | Salem - CollegeShine","description":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem is a government arts & science college in Gorimedu, Salem established in 1972. The only government women''s college.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Women-Salem-collegshine_2_11zon.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem | Salem - CollegeShine","description":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem is a government arts & science college in Gorimedu, Salem established in 1972. The only government women''s college.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Women-Salem-collegshine_2_11zon.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem","shortName":"GACW Salem","tagline":"The only government women''s college in Salem district","category":"arts-science","type":"Degree College (Women)","ownership":"Government","established":"1972","location":"Gorimedu, Salem","district":"Salem","address":"Government Arts College for Women, Yercaud Main Road, Gorimedu, Salem - 636008, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Government+Arts+College+for+Women+Salem","mapQuery":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem, Tamil Nadu 636008","website":"https://govtwomencollegeslm8.org/","phone":null,"email":null,"image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Women-Salem-collegshine_2_11zon.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/r13dOq4DkW8?si=sn0B_BN5EHwIfgeY","affiliation":"Periyar University, Salem","accreditation":["NAAC A (3rd Cycle, Re-accredited)"],"about":"Government Arts College for Women, Salem is the only government college for women in the entire Salem district, built on a 14.71-acre campus at the foothills of the Yercaud hill resort. The college began as a government men''s college in 1972 and was converted into a women''s college in 1979. Since then it has steadily added programmes, from B.A. and B.Sc. courses in the 1970s and 80s to B.Com in 1981, M.Sc. Mathematics and B.Sc. Computer Science in 1997, and BCA, M.Sc. Chemistry, M.Sc. Computer Science and M.A. Tamil Literature by 2010. It is affiliated to Periyar University, Salem and has been re-accredited with an ''A'' grade by NAAC in its third cycle.\\n\\nWith around 3,500 students and a faculty of 150, the college maintains a library holding 68,857 books, along with separate hostel facilities of 125-bed capacity each for boys and girls (a combined 250 originally provided by the Government) and departmental laboratories including a Language Lab and a Computer Literacy Programme (CLP) lab. Per the NIRF 2025 report, a total of 403 undergraduate and 35 postgraduate students were placed, at reported median packages of roughly Rs 2.25-2.30 LPA. The college ranks in the 151-200 band in NIRF 2025 and continues to serve as the primary access point to higher education for women across Salem city and its suburbs.","highlights":["Only government women''s college in Salem district","Started as a men''s college in 1972, converted to women''s college in 1979","NAAC A grade (3rd Cycle, re-accredited)","NIRF 2025 ranking: 151-200 band","Library holds 68,857 books"],"departments":[{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"}],"facilities":["Boys hostel (125 capacity)","Girls hostel (125 capacity)","Language Lab","CLP (Computer Literacy Programme) lab with LCD facilities","Auditorium","Canteen","IT infrastructure"],"placementRate":0,"avgPackage":null,"highestPackage":null,"placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":["Merit-based admission per Tamil Nadu Government norms","Affiliated with Periyar University and recognised by UGC","10+2 required for BA/BSc/BCom/BCA UG entry","Relevant Bachelor''s degree required for MA/MSc/MCom/MPhil/PhD entry"],"scholarships":[],"events":[],"distanceInfo":{"Salem Junction Railway Station":"~8 km","Salem New Bus Stand":"~6 km"},"hostelFeatures":["Separate boys'' and girls'' hostels","125-bed capacity each"],"technicalClubs":[],"culturalClubs":[],"communityService":[]}'),
