,"NAAC Quality Initiative","IQAC Established","NIRF 2024 Data Submitted"],"about":"Government Arts and Science College, Hosur was established by the Government of Tamil Nadu in 2013 and is located at Mathigiri, Hosur, in Krishnagiri District. The official college website states that the campus is situated approximately 2 km from Hosur Railway Station and 4 km from the Hosur Bus Stand. The campus extends across 5.33 acres and accommodates academic facilities, playground areas and gardens. The college serves students from Hosur and surrounding areas through undergraduate and postgraduate education.\\n\\nThe college offers undergraduate programmes including B.A. Tamil, B.A. English, B.Sc. Botany, B.Sc. Chemistry, B.Sc. Mathematics, B.Sc. Physics, B.Sc. Computer Science, B.Sc. Statistics, B.Com., B.Com. Computer Applications and B.B.A. Its postgraduate programmes include M.A. Tamil, M.A. English, M.Sc. Mathematics, M.Sc. Computer Science and M.Com. The official 2025-26 and 2026-27 admission pages confirm department-wise admission and merit-based selection under Tamil Nadu Government reservation rules. NIRF 2024 submitted data reports 1,386 undergraduate students and 134 postgraduate students, totalling 1,520 students in the reporting year.","highlights":["Established by Tamil Nadu Government in 2013","Located at Mathigiri, Hosur","5.33-acre campus","Approximately 2 km from Hosur Railway Station","Approximately 4 km from Hosur Bus Stand","Government Arts and Science College","Affiliated to Periyar University, Salem","11 academic departments","16 UG and PG programmes","1,520 students reported in NIRF 2024 data","UG and PG programmes available","Computer Science and Computer Applications programmes"],"departments":[{"name":"Tamil","level":"PG"},{"name":"English","level":"PG"},{"name":"Botany","level":"UG"},{"name":"Chemistry","level":"UG"},{"name":"Mathematics","level":"PG"},{"name":"Physics","level":"UG"},{"name":"Computer Science","level":"PG"},{"name":"Statistics","leve