on":["Government Institution","Periyar University Affiliated","UGC Recognised"],"about":"Government Arts and Science College, Pennagaram was established in 2010 as a Periyar University Constituent College of Arts and Science to expand access to higher education for students in the Pennagaram region. The institution initially functioned from Government Higher Secondary School premises at Paparapatty and later moved to its permanent campus at Mamarathupallam. The dedicated college building was inaugurated on 23 September 2014 through video conference by the then Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu, J. Jayalalithaa. The college subsequently became a Government Arts and Science College under the Government of Tamil Nadu.\\n\\nThe college is located in Pennagaram Taluk of Dharmapuri District and is affiliated with Periyar University, Salem. It is a co-educational government institution offering undergraduate programmes in Tamil, Commerce, Computer Science, English and Mathematics. The Tamil Nadu Government''s 2026 TNGASA information lists five current UG programmes with sanctioned strengths of 60 for B.A. Tamil, 60 for B.Com., 40 for B.Sc. Computer Science, 60 for B.A. English and 60 for B.Sc. Mathematics. The institution also has welfare hostel facilities, academic infrastructure and student-development activities.","highlights":["Established in 2010","Government Arts and Science College","Periyar University Affiliated","15.96-Acre Campus","Co-Educational Institution","Five Current Undergraduate Programmes","Government Welfare Hostel Support","Computer Science Education","Mathematics Education","Commerce Education","English Education","Tamil Education"],"departments":[{"name":"B.A. Tamil","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Com. Commerce","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Computer Science","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. English","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Mathematics","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Campus Wi-Fi"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"College Library"},{"icon":"ti-