zed","Periyar University Affiliated","2(f) & 12(B) Recognized","IIC 3.5 Star Rating"],"about":"Bharathiyar Arts and Science College for Women (BASCW) was established in 1997 by Sri Sakthi Educational Trust at Deviyakurichi, Thalaivasal, Salem District. The institution is dedicated to women''s higher education and follows the educational vision inspired by Mahakavi Bharathiyar, with a particular focus on empowering rural women through quality education, practical exposure, ethical values and scientific thinking. The college is affiliated to Periyar University, Salem, and has developed a broad academic structure covering Arts, Science, Commerce, Management, Computer Applications and Biological Sciences.\\n\\nThe college currently provides undergraduate, postgraduate and research programmes. Its official website lists programmes including B.Lit. Tamil, B.A. English, B.A. History, B.Com, B.Com (CA), B.Com (IT), B.B.A, B.C.A, B.Sc Computer Science, B.Sc Computer Science with Artificial Intelligence, B.Sc Computer Science with Cyber Security, B.Sc Chemistry, B.Sc Physics, B.Sc Mathematics, B.Sc Statistics, B.Sc Botany, B.Sc Zoology, B.Sc Nutrition and Dietetics, B.Sc Fashion Technology, B.Sc Microbiology and B.Sc Biotechnology, together with postgraduate and Ph.D. programmes. The campus provides academic blocks, laboratories, library, hostel, transport, canteen, auditorium, sports, placement support, research facilities and student-development cells.","highlights":["Established in 1997","Women-focused higher education institution","Sri Sakthi Educational Trust Management","Affiliated to Periyar University","NAAC A+ Grade","UGC Recognized","Autonomous Institution","31 Academic Programmes","16 Department Areas","30,853 Library Books","2,000 Book Bank Books","100 Hostel Rooms","20 Digital Library Computers","80 National and International Journals","IIC 3.5 Star Rating","Research and Innovation Facilities"],"departments":[{"name":"Tamil","level":"PhD"},{"name":"English","leve