University Constituent College","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","NAAC and IQAC Cell","UGC Recognised University Affiliated Institution"],"about":"Periyar University College of Arts and Science, Harur was established by the Government of Tamil Nadu through G.O. (Perm) No. 35 dated 18 July 2011. The college became a constituent college of Periyar University and was affiliated on 22 July 2011. It was established to provide accessible higher education to students in the educationally backward Harur Taluk. The college is situated near Harur Government Hospital on Morappur Main Road and operates from its own three-acre campus.\\n\\nThe college began its academic journey in 2011 with B.A. English, B.Com., B.Sc. Botany and B.Sc. Computer Science. B.Sc. Mathematics was introduced in 2016, while B.A. Tamil and M.A. English were introduced in 2017. The official Periyar University profile records 953 students studying in these programmes. The institution focuses on providing affordable, student-friendly and accessible education for rural and remote students, with emphasis on knowledge, skills, self-employment, social responsibility and higher education.\\n\\nThe college provides academic facilities including Botany, Computer Science and Chemistry laboratories, a library with 2,832 volumes, physical education and yoga training, sports participation and several student-support and extension cells. Its official profile lists NSS, Youth Red Cross, Red Ribbon Club, Anti-Ragging Cell, Placement Cell, IQAC and NAAC, Students Welfare and Services Cell, Grievance and Redressal Cell, Alumni Cell, SWAYAM and MOOCs, Equal Opportunity Cell, Discipline Committee, Slow Learners Coaching Programme, Campus Green and Cleanliness Committee and Competitive Exams Coaching Programme.","highlights":["Established in 2011","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","Constituent College of Periyar University","Located in Harur, Dharmapuri District","Three-acre own campus","953 students recorded on of