iyur","openGraph":{"title":"Government Arts and Science College - CollegeShine","description":"Government Arts and Science College (Co-Education), Anthiyur is a government of tamil nadu arts & science college in Anthiyur established in 2022. Quality.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-and-Science-College-Co-Education-Anthiyur-collegshine_10_11zon-150x150.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Government Arts and Science College - CollegeShine","description":"Government Arts and Science College (Co-Education), Anthiyur is a government of tamil nadu arts & science college in Anthiyur established in 2022. Quality.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-and-Science-College-Co-Education-Anthiyur-collegshine_10_11zon-150x150.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Government Arts and Science College (Co-Education), Anthiyur","shortName":"GASC Anthiyur","tagline":"Quality Higher Education for All Sections of Society","category":"arts-science","type":"Government Arts and Science College","ownership":"Government of Tamil Nadu","established":2022,"location":"Anthiyur","district":"Erode","address":"Government Arts and Science College, Anthiyur - 638501, Erode District, Tamil Nadu","mapLink":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Government+Arts+and+Science+College+Anthiyur","mapQuery":"Government Arts and Science College, Anthiyur 638501","website":"https://gascanthiyur.in","phone":"04256-262230","email":"gascanthiyur@gmail.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-and-Science-College-Co-Education-Anthiyur-collegshine_10_11zon-150x150.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/dQw4w9WgXcQ","affiliation":"Bharathiar University, Coimbatore","accreditation":["Government Arts and Science College","Affiliated to Bharathiar University","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","UGC-Norm Qualified Faculty"],"about":"Government Arts and Science College, Anthiyur affiliated to Bharathiar University, Coimbatore was established in 2022 and started functioning in the academic year 2022-2023. The institution was established with the vision of providing quality higher education to all sections of society, with particular emphasis on students from economically and socially disadvantaged backgrounds. The college is situated in the Government Boys Higher Secondary School campus and occupies a 10-acre area in Anthiyur town.\\n\\nThe college began with five undergraduate degree programmes in Tamil Literature, English Literature, Commerce, Computer Science and Mathematics. The institution has developed a student strength of around 500 and provides 10 well-ventilated classrooms, science laboratories, a well-equipped library with internet facility, 150 Mbps fibre-connected Wi-Fi, 24-hour CCTV surveillance and separate parking facilities. The college also provides sports activities, Naan Mudhalvan skill development training, NSS, NCC, Youth Red Cross, placement and career guidance, Women Cell, Entrepreneurship Development Cell and Anti-Drug Cell activities.","highlights":["10-Acre Campus","Approximately 500 Students","Five Undergraduate Programmes","3,000+ Library Books","150 Mbps Wi-Fi Connectivity","24-Hour CCTV Surveillance","Well-Ventilated Classrooms","Science Laboratory Facilities","Computer Science Laboratory","Career Guidance and Placement Cell","Naan Mudhalvan Skill Training","NSS and NCC Activities"],"departments":[{"name":"B.A. Tamil Literature","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. English Literature","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Com.","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Mathematics","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Computer Science","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"150 Mbps Campus Wi-Fi"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"3,000+ Book Library"},{"icon":"ti-desktop","name":"Computer Laboratory"},{"icon":"ti-blackboard","name":"Well-Ventilated Classrooms"},{"icon":"ti-world","name":"Internet-Enabled Library"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-cctv","name":"24-Hour CCTV Surveillance"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Academic Seminar Activities"},{"icon":"ti-crown","name":"Career Guidance and Placement Cell"},{"icon":"ti-light-bulb","name":"Naan Mudhalvan Training"},{"icon":"ti-users","name":"NSS and NCC Activities"},{"icon":"ti-car","name":"Separate Student Parking"}],"placementRate":80,"avgPackage":"Career Opportunities Available","highestPackage":"Recruitment Opportunities Available","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Online Application","desc":"Candidates apply through the Tamil Nadu Government Arts and Science Colleges admission process and the college admission system."},{"title":"Eligibility Verification","desc":"Applicants must have passed the Higher Secondary Plus Two examination or an equivalent recognised qualification and satisfy the prescribed course requirements."},{"title":"Merit Preparation","desc":"Eligible applicants are considered through the prescribed admission and rank-list process followed by the Government Arts and Science Colleges."},{"title":"Special Quota Counselling","desc":"Special reservation categories including differently abled, sports, NCC, ex-service personnel and other notified categories are considered through the prescribed counselling process."},{"title":"Document Verification","desc":"Candidates present the required educational certificates, transfer certificate, community certificate and other supporting documents during admission."},{"title":"Seat Confirmation","desc":"Candidates complete the prescribed admission formalities and fee payment to confirm their allotted seat."}],"scholarships":["Tamil Nadu Government Scholarships","SC/ST Post-Matric Scholarship","BC/MBC/DNC Scholarship","Minority Welfare Scholarship","First Graduate Scholarship","Differently Abled Stu